---
import PolicyLayout from "../layouts/PolicyLayout.astro";
import { business } from "../siteConstants/business";
---

<PolicyLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="How deposits, milestone payments and refunds work for software development services."
>
  <p>
    This Refund Policy applies to all software development services provided by {business.name} ({business.ssmNo}) ("we", "us"), including website and web
    application development, custom systems, integrations, maintenance and
    consulting. Payments are processed by our payment gateway, CHIP
    (chip-in.asia).
  </p>

  <h2>1. Quotations and deposits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Every project starts with a written quotation that sets out the scope,
      price, payment schedule and estimated timeline.
    </li>
    <li>
      Most projects require a deposit before work begins. The deposit secures
      your place in our schedule and covers initial discovery, planning and
      setup.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you cancel in writing <strong>before any work has started</strong>,
      the deposit is refunded in full.
    </li>
    <li>
      Once work has started, the deposit is non-refundable, except where we are
      unable to deliver the agreed work (see section 3).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Milestone payments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Larger projects are split into milestones. Each milestone payment covers
      the work for that milestone only.
    </li>
    <li>
      A milestone payment is refundable if we do not deliver that milestone, or
      if the delivered work does not materially meet the agreed specification
      and we cannot correct it within the revision period described in our <a href="/shipping-policy">Delivery &amp; Return Policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Milestones that you have accepted, or that are deemed accepted, are
      non-refundable.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. When you are entitled to a refund</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We cancel the project or are unable to deliver: you receive a refund of
      all payments for work not yet delivered.
    </li>
    <li>
      You cancel before work starts: full refund of amounts paid.
    </li>
    <li>
      You cancel after work starts: refund of any amount paid in advance for
      work not yet performed, less the deposit and the value of work completed
      up to the date of cancellation.
    </li>
    <li>
      Duplicate or incorrect charges: refunded in full.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. What is not refundable</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Work that has been delivered and accepted.</li>
    <li>
      Third-party costs paid on your behalf, such as domain names, hosting,
      software licences, app store fees and paid APIs.
    </li>
    <li>
      Delays or extra costs caused by late feedback, missing content or
      changes in scope requested by you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> within 14
    days of the relevant charge or delivery, with your invoice or payment
    reference number and the reason for the request.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Timelines</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We acknowledge your request within 3 business days.</li>
    <li>We give you a decision within 7 business days of receiving it.</li>
    <li>Approved refunds are issued within 7 business days of approval.</li>
    <li>
      Your bank, card issuer or e-wallet provider may take a further 7 to 14
      business days to show the refund on your statement.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Refund method</h2>
  <p>
    Refunds are made to the <strong>original payment method</strong> through
    CHIP, whether that was a credit or debit card, FPX online banking, an
    e-wallet or another method offered at checkout. If a refund to the original
    method is not possible (for example, the card or account has been closed),
    we will refund by bank transfer to an account in the payer's name.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or see our <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
